Z||000000||Bigfieroman||06-18-2001||04:04 PM||||Will the 3.4 from the 91-97 Lumina, the 96-97 Monte Carlo, the 91-96 Grand Prix, and the 99-current Grand Am work?  They are all front drivers, and there may be no need to drill the starter holes as in the Camaro.  A local Chevrolet dealer said that all these engines are based on the same block as our 2.8!  Please feed me a little info!<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||06-18-2001||04:16 PM||||I dunno, maybe it'll fit. All I kow is that as long as 16 year olds get to drive, there will never be a shortage of V6 f-body donors. Just need to unwrap it from that bridge abutment.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||06-18-2001||04:41 PM||||It's been done by fierosound. These engines have a roller camshaft in them. They also have aluminum heads and different pistons. If you want to use your fiero intake and heads you have to change the pistons. This is his website. <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
